  "providerDifferences": [
    "Chromium keeps an edited active view until reselection; WebCore applies the edit immediately. Both keep a cleared former view inactive after editing it (0027 GREEN).",
    "Native currentView/useCurrentView are Available; Chromium reports NotExposed.",
    "WebCoreHost.SelectSvgView takes fragment text without # (\"#half\" selects nothing); Chromium location.hash accepts both forms. Browser requests update URL/history/:target; native selection does not.",
    "WebKit currentScale changes page zoom and leaves the content CSS size unchanged (currentTranslate then divides by the zoom); Chromium zooms SVG content.",
    "A new begin on a frozen SMIL animation takes effect during a paused seek in Chromium; WebCore keeps the frozen value. Fresh delayed begins/ends agree.",
    "Fable erases Some null to None; the browser treats it as attribute removal, and nullArg surfaces as Error rather than ArgumentNullException."
  ],
  "initialFailures": [
    "Async.RunSynchronously ran fixtures on a pool thread: InvalidOperationException off host thread; fixed by StartImmediateAsTask on the host thread.",
    "Native delayed begin after endElement on a frozen animation kept 59.97 at the 8 s seek (Chromium 20); retained as an explicit provider flag, with a separate fresh delayed-begin check.",
    "HTML-document selection surfaced as NotSupportedException \"not supported by this WebCore build\"; SelectSvgView now reports that an SVG main document is required.",
    "Fable rejected System.Double.IsFinite; replaced by IsNaN/IsInfinity.",
    "Browser null-argument name and Some null erasure (above)."
  ],
